# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the NextToonz unit tests.
#
# Used by workflow_sanitizers.yml (LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=<this file>).
# Each entry is a leak in the library that is known and not fixed yet; the
# numbers refer to doc/nexttoonz_known_issues.md. LeakSanitizer matches the
# text after "leak:" against the functions of the allocation's stack, and
# also drops everything reachable from a suppressed allocation.
#
# Do not add an entry to make a new leak go away: fix it, or record it in
# the known issues first. Remove an entry when its issue is fixed.

# 10: TVectorImage::removeStroke() never frees the stroke's VIStroke wrapper.
# Only the three tests that call it are let through, so that any other leak
# of a wrapper still shows.
leak:TVectorImage_AddGetRemoveStrokes_Test
leak:TVectorImage_RemovingTheClosedStrokeRemovesItsRegion_Test
leak:TVectorImage_CloneImageIsIndependent_Test

# 20: createStandardCleanupPalette() returns a palette with a reference that
# nobody releases; every CleanupParameters (one per TSceneProperties) leaks
# its palette.
leak:createStandardCleanupPalette

# 21: TOutputProperties::getFileFormatProperties() replaces the property
# group of a format without deleting the old one.
leak:TOutputProperties::getFileFormatProperties

# 22: TXshZeraryFxColumn and its TXshZeraryFxLevel hold a reference on each
# other, so no zerary column is ever freed, nor the fx inside it.
leak:TXshZeraryFxColumn::TXshZeraryFxColumn

# 23: objects that live until the process exits but are not reachable from
# a global by then: the measures and units of TMeasureManager, the generator
# registered by a static initialiser in stdfx/shaderfx.cpp, and in tcomposer
# the writer properties registered by Tiio::defineStd() and the plugin
# loader's thread object.
leak:TMeasureManager::
leak:SCMDelegateGenerator::SCMDelegateGenerator
leak:Tiio::defineStd
leak:PluginLoader::load_entries

# 24: the fxs ported from Toonz 4.6 (artContourFx, blendTzFx, calligraphicFx,
# outBorderFx, and applyCmappedFx in toonzlib/tcolumnfx.cpp) pass their
# parameters as C strings made by strsave(), which nothing frees.
leak:strsave

# 25: a TLevelWriter does not free the property group it is given, and
# LevelUpdater hands it a fresh clone every time it opens one.
leak:LevelUpdater::open

# Not ours: Qt's xcb event thread can still be inside libxcb when tcomposer
# exits under xvfb-run.
leak:xcb_wait_for_event
